  "place": "Qingzhou",
  "blurb": [
    "A Yellow Turban host has thrown a ring around Qingzhou, camped in the ripe millet right up to the gate, and Governor Gong Jing cannot hold the walls forever. Liu Bei comes with his own company, Jian Yong at his shoulder and the magistrate Zou Jing and his archers beside him. It is not enough, and Liu Bei knows it.",
    "He will give ground on purpose. The rebels are in the habit of chasing anyone who runs, and Guan Yu and Zhang Fei are waiting behind the wooded ridges on either side of the road with the rest of the company. Draw the chief into the pocket, keep Liu Bei alive until the horns sound, and when the governor opens his gate the rebels will find themselves with a wall at their backs."
  ],
